            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "special+holonomy#Leung02"}> Leung 02
              )
          %h3#as_quaternionic_manifolds As quaternionic manifolds
          #QuaternionKaehlermanifoldsAreQuaternionicManifolds.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} quaternion-Kähler manifolds
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+manifolds"} quaternionic manifolds
            %p
              By definition, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} quaternion-Kähler manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+group"} holonomy group
              contained in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+group"} direct product group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%28n%29"} Sp(n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29"} Sp(1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              on the holonomy bundle as
              = succeed "-free." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+G-structure"} torsion
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+manifold"} quaternionic manifold
            %p
              Such extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mtext quat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_\text{quat}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              however is not unique, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mtext quat
                    %mo +
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_\text{quat} + \mathcal{S}
              is another Sp(n)Sp(1)-preserving connection, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              is a (1, 2)-tensor such that for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}(p)
              takes values in the first
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prolongation"} prolongation
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
          %h3#AsEinsteinManifolds As Einstein manifolds
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} quaternion-Kähler manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifolds"} Einstein manifolds
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Cortes05"} Cortés 05, slide 22
          %h3#characteristic_classes Characteristic classes
          #CharacteristicClassesForSpin5Spin3Structure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              8 with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+structure"} Spin structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
              moreover admits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
              for
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\;G =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%28n%29.Sp%281%29"} Sp(2).Sp(1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%288%29"} SO(8)
            %p
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+class"} Euler class
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi χ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Pontryagin+class"} second Pontryagin class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
              and the
              = succeed "-square" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_1)^2
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Pontryagin+class"} first Pontryagin class
              of the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              are related by
            #eq:EulerClassInTermsOfPontryagin.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 8
                    %mi χ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 4
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    8 \chi
                    \\;=\;
                    4 p_2 - (p_1)^2
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CadekVanzura98"}> Čadek-Vanžura 98, Theorem 8.1 with Remark 8.2
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The same conclusion
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EulerClassInTermsOfPontryagin"} (1)
              also holds for
              = succeed "-structure," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(7)
              %a{:href => "Spin7-manifold#CharacteristicClassesForSpinStructure"} there
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field+tadpole+cancellation"} C-field tadpole cancellation
          %h3#reduction_to_hyperkhler_structure Reduction to hyper-Kähler structure
          %p
            A quaternion-Kähler manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyper-Kähler manifold
            = succeed "-structure," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n) \hookrightarrow Sp(n)\cdot Sp(1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+curvature"} scalar curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            being an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(g) = 0
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Amann09"} Amann 09, below Def. 1.5
          %h3#PositiveQuaternionKaehlerManifolds Positive quaternion-Kähler manifolds
          #PositiveQuaternionKaehlerManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A quaternion-Kähler manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
              is called
              %em positive
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesically+complete"} geodesically complete
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+curvature"} scalar curvature
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
                  by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
                  being an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein manifold
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive number
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(g) \gt 0
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salamon82"}> Salamon 82, Section 6
            , see e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Amann09"} Amann 09, Def. 1.5
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifold
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PositiveQuaternionKaehlerManifold"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salamon82"}> Salamon 82, p. 158 (16 of 29)
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifold
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PositiveQuaternionKaehlerManifold"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salamon82"}> Salamon 82, Theorem 6.6
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(X)
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifolds
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PositiveQuaternionKaehlerManifold"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LeBrunSalamon94"}> LeBrun-Salamon 94, Theorem 0.1
            )
          #WoldSpacesArePositiveQuaternionKaehler.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              (
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolf+spaces"} Wolf spaces
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifolds
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolf+space"} Wolf space
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifold
          %p
            In fact the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolf+spaces"} Wolf spaces
            are the only known examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifold
            (which is not hyper-Kähler ?!), as of today (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Salamon82"} Salamon 82, Section 5
          %p
            This leads to the
            %strong conjecture
            that in every dimension, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolf+spaces"} Wolf spaces
            are the only
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} positive quaternion-Kähler manifolds
          %p
            The conjecture has been proven for the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
                (Hitchin)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 8
                (
                %a{:href => "#PoonSalamon91"}> Poon-Salamon 91
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#LeBrunSalamon94"} LeBrun-Salamon 94
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p The archetypical example is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+projective+plane"} quaternionic projective plane
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,\mathbb{H}P^2
          %p
            This is the first of the list of examples of spaces that are both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion-K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} quaternion-Kähler manifolds
            as well as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spaces"} symmetric spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolf+spaces"} Wolf spaces
          %p
            See around Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WoldSpacesArePositiveQuaternionKaehler"}
            above.
          %p
            %br/
